{"id": "ece29ca5-4ae9-4520-80c5-ff557217f76b", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:52:43.553807", "source": "user", "parent_id": "8ecfd141-5238-4b16-9579-78bfc7ac36d2", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task; no execution of LLM queries is required. Please begin with the initial_inspection step only. Do not draft the full experiment yet. Specifically, I need you to deliver three things in this round: (1) a brief inventory of anything already present in the working directory /workspace (files, any prior notes, seed data, scripts) by listing and summarizing them; if the directory is empty or irrelevant, state that plainly; (2) a concise proposed experimental approach to test whether LLMs exhibit a directional bias on real-world factual celebrity parent-child data — namely, higher accuracy in the parent-given-child-answered direction (i.e., retrieving the parent given a child) than in the child-given-parent-answered direction (i.e., retrieving the child given a parent) — covering: stimulus construction, item selection criteria, prompt template(s), LLM candidate(s) and how they will be specified as design choices (not executed), scoring metric, controls, and statistical analysis plan, including effect size and power considerations relevant to a paired directional comparison; (3) a short list of consequential assumptions and open uncertainties I should resolve at approach_review (e.g., entity curation source, handling of multi-child/multi-marriage cases, prompt phrasing choices, mitigation of memorization confounds, what counts as a 'correct' parent/child, model selection rationale, what evidence will be reported even though execution is not required). Keep this round strictly to inspection + proposed approach + assumptions/uncertainties. Await my approval before producing the full deliverable.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"For real-world factual data on celebrity parent-child relationships, LLMs will exhibit a directional bias by accurately retrieving a parent when given a child’s name, but will underperform when trying to retrieve the child given the parent.\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
